# rpmlint findings this package accepts, with the reason for each.
#
# Everything not listed here stays fatal in CI. The list is deliberately
# narrow -- each entry names the specific finding rather than switching a
# whole check off -- because a lint that cannot fail is not a lint.
#
# addFilter() rather than a TOML `Filters` list: an rpmlintrc file is read in
# this older form even by rpmlint 2, which loads a `.toml` file as TOML and
# anything else as this. Written as TOML it was accepted without complaint,
# reported as loaded, and had no effect at all.

# rpmlint's dictionary does not carry this plural, and %description uses it
# because durations are what half the tool computes. Only this word is
# excused: any other misspelling in %description still fails, which is what
# the check is worth having for.
addFilter(r"spelling-error .*'[Dd]urations'")

# Source1 is the vendored crates. A Fedora build root has no network, so the
# dependencies are built in from a tarball made from Cargo.lock at package
# time -- there is no URL it could have. rust2rpm's output carries the same
# finding for the same reason.
addFilter(r"invalid-url Source1:")
